# Oh-My-Research — MCP API keys / tokens.
#
# Two ways to provide these:
#   1. Export in your shell profile (~/.zshrc, ~/.bashrc) — wins over .env,
#      and is the ONLY way HTTP-transport MCPs (github, huggingface) can read
#      them, because the plugin's .env loader only runs for the stdio servers.
#   2. Copy this file to .env in the project where you run Claude Code, then
#      fill in the stdio-server keys. Missing keys = that server fails to
#      start; the others still work.
#
# Stdio (.env fallback works):
#   EXA_API_KEY            https://dashboard.exa.ai/api-keys
#   TAVILY_API_KEY         https://app.tavily.com/home
#   BRAVE_API_KEY          https://api.search.brave.com/app/keys
#
# HTTP (shell env required):
#   GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN   https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
#   HF_TOKEN                       https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens

EXA_API_KEY=
TAVILY_API_KEY=
BRAVE_API_KEY=
GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=
HF_TOKEN=
